Wll, I've got an on-line description of the FILES-11 ODS-2 filesystem (as of
1978) that I could e-mail to you.  It describes what's supposed to be on the
disk in order for it to be mountable.  It also describes the layout of file
headers, which is enough information for you to be able to search the entire
disk for file headers, keeping track of what blocks are actually used by files
that still have valid file headers on the disk.  Using that information, you
MIGHT be able to construct what will look to VMS like valid versions of, say,
the file header for BITMAP.SYS, etc.  Before you do anything else, though, you
should probably take a physical backup of the disk.
